  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2xc6e3yec2m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Not that AI discourse has ever been great, but \"of course LLMs are good at math\" both misses that \"good at math\" is an *slight* understatement in the context of solving the Reimann Hypothesis & also ignores the fact that LLMs were not actually \"good at math\" until very recent breakthroughs.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2xc6e3yec2m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T04:29:03.646Z",
      "likes": 237,
      "replies": 10,
      "reposts": 17,
      "score": 7.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 13.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2x4fwduu22m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Yes, it is reasonable to expect AI models struggle more with unverifiable domains, but I do think it is worth noting that we also see very large gains in domains without automatic verification as well\n\nHere are humans evaluations of AI in writing, business problems, design, and doing freelance tasks",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2x4fwduu22m",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T02:45:55.208Z",
      "likes": 86,
      "replies": 6,
      "reposts": 4,
      "score": 6.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 15.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2yixn4gps2g",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Walmart seems determined not to make the same mistake with agentic commerce that it did with ecommerce. While Amazon is blocking agents, Walmart is embracing them - quite a reversal.\n\nAnd the new data from Stripe suggests agentic shopping may actually be kicking off & is suprisingly sticky.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3n2yixn4gps2g",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T16:03:14.146Z",
      "likes": 49,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 6.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.7,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2wyrdmla22n",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I don't hesitate to block. undisclosed bots. People that are clearly using AI to write posts will probably be blocked too. \n\nI'm on social media to interact with people. The \"social\" part. If I want to talk to an AI, I have Claude and ChatGPT apps for that. \n\nYou're just wasting my time, otherwise.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2wyrdmla22n",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-23T01:40:43.257Z",
      "likes": 22,
      "replies": 0,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 16.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2vshrz37226",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "The Alignment Research Center is super sketch. A handful of people who started a charitable organization whose “benefit” to society is saving humanity from extinction by AI. Funded almost exclusively by likeminded philanthropists, like Sam Bankman-Fried.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2vshrz37226",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-22T14:15:20.396Z",
      "likes": 1,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 3.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 0.6,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 27.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3n2vouuqqkc26",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Or that everyone must put prompt injection attacks in their papers. Or that all reviewers use LLMs that are equally susceptible to prompt injection attacks. Everyone needs to play by the same rules, whatever they are, and right now that isn’t happening (and also, AI review is not “peer” review).",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3n2vouuqqkc26",
